From 9213b785de645f47ef25d8d53b5b940fce8a4347 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:01:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] feat(ops): publish the request-body ceiling through
 Redis, file as fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

request_body_limit_service shared the upload ceiling between Uvicorn workers
by writing request-body-limit.json into the TLS volume — IPC that only
reaches workers on the same host. The ceiling is now SET in Redis
(`alpharouter:request_body_limit_mb`) by publish_request_body_limit_mb_async
and re-read by RequestBodyLimitMiddleware every 5 s
(refresh_request_body_limit_from_redis, 250 ms timeout, 30 s back-off after a
failure). The state file is still written and stays the fallback, so a
single-host install without Redis reachability behaves exactly as before.
Both TLS-edge publishers (transfer-limit save, HTTPS activate) use the async
variant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
